ts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T01:37:07-07:00","id":567592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/567387-second-edition-elementals?p=567588#post567588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Basiclly, new Elementals are <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=i5mBYxDUubs\" target=\"_blank\">modern Lara Croft</a>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Or <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dsVv6Kkp3R0\" target=\"_blank\">Oliver Queen, a.k.a. Green Arrow</a>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm thinking more V from V For Vendetta; he's got to be a pretty quintessential example of a character who abandons his ego in order to survive. Is it possible to be an anarchy elemental? :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 06-25-2015, 04:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T02:16:49-07:00","id":567604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/567387-second-edition-elementals?p=567556#post567556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They don't need magical powers for that. They escaped on their own. That's something they've got, and that can't be taken away from them. Nobody gave it to them; that was all them.</div> </div> </div> </div>So Seemings have purely mental and cosmetic effects?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T02:25:35-07:00","id":567608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/567387-second-edition-elementals?p=567604#post567604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So Seemings have purely mental and cosmetic effects?</div> </div> </div> </div>They'll also affect affinity Contracts. I wouldn't downplay free Clarity as &quot;purely mental&quot;. It's pretty significant. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T02:40:31-07:00","id":567611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/567387-second-edition-elementals?p=567608#post567608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They'll also affect affinity Contracts. I wouldn't downplay free Clarity as &quot;purely mental&quot;. It's pretty significant.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, Clarity is more than merely a measure of a Changeling's sanity?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T04:05:19-07:00","id":567623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/567387-second-edition-elementals?p=567500#post567500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So as an Elemental, if I do something completely bonkers and I can justify the reason for it, I get clarity point? Sounds like these guys are going to be fun!</div> </div> </div> </div>Not only that, but the weakness is a way for the Storyteller to slap a Chaotic Stupid player upside the head.<br /> <br /> Congrats, David A. Hill, you've made controllable fishmalks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T04:11:22-07:00","id":567626,"title":"","content":"I'm really having trouble understanding how Elementals escaped. Could someone provide examples; lets say the following three durance:<br /> <br /> Slave in the underground mines.<br /> Cotton picker in a southern plantation.<br /> Turned into a loyal robot in a space opera.<br /> <br /> For those can someone describe an escape that would create an Elemental?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T04:34:00-07:00","id":567638,"title":"","content":"I think Elementals escape by causing choas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T05:03:06-07:00","id":567683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Character Concepts</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">She spent her life holding it in, hiding what she knew herself to be, to protect her friends and her family. Things are different now. She\u2019ll burn them all with the bitter cold inside of her. She\u2019ll create her own world of ice and snow where she\u2019s completely free, and who cares who freezes to death in the process.</div> </div> </div> </div> Elsa no!<br /> <br /> Anyway, I like this. Manages to keep the original Seeming's flavor while still being unique.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T05:07:34-07:00","id":567687,"title":"","content":"I too have problems with understanding how they escaped. Beasts abandoned social constructs and went wild like animals. Darklings sacrificed somebody else. Fairest accepted responsibility and became leaders and patrons to others. We don't know about Wizened, but it could be something about using brain/skill/craft to escape.But elementals are unclear.<br /> I do, however, like how they got rid of their ego and understood they're just one thing more in universe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6005-coolcat12345","name":"coolcat12345","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T05:57:01-07:00","id":567784,"title":"","content":"The answers seems to lie in the question of why the Elemental is there in the first place. They're a slave in the underground mine because, I dunno, they're trying to prove they're capable of doing hard, degrading work to the Keeper? Escape, in such a case, could simply be allowing yourself to understand that you don't <i>have</i> to prove that. (Realizing that you've <i>already</i> proved it, I think, belongs to another Seeming.) Their chains are forged from pieces of their ego, and they break when their ego falls away.<br /> <br /> ...which, it occurs to me, sounds very Buddhist. The Elemental durance comes about because of the three fires: passion, aversion, and ignorance: and you free yourself by discarding them to attain nirvana.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T07:24:12-07:00","id":567888,"title":"","content":"I don't like the idea that you can only become an Elemental if the Durance allows it. I can think of a way the mine slave who's kept in place because of chains and guards could become any other seeming:<br /> <br /> Beast - crawl through a tunnel so filthy not even escape tempts other slaves.<br /> Ogre - toughen up until you're able to break the chains and take the guards in a fight.<br /> Fairest - inspire the other slaves into rebellion.<br /> Darkling - betray another slave in order to escape.<br /> <br /> But an Elemental. No clue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T07:26:55-07:00","id":567892,"title":"","content":"Become one with the darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T07:31:16-07:00","id":567896,"title":"","content":"So am I the only one who thinks their blessing essentially turns them all into Sherlock Holmes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1746-pants-o-doom","name":"Pants O Doom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T07:42:04-07:00","id":567921,"title":"","content":"I was thinking more along the lines of a baron munchausen type who weaves their lives into a story.<br /> <br /> If talecrafting works anything like it used to, literally weaving their lives into a story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T07:46:26-07:00","id":567926,"title":"","content":"Raven, you don't see how someone becoming part of a living world and effectively ripping themselves off and running the hell away akin to the skin on your left knee just yanking itself off and slopping across the floor is an effective form of escape?<br /> <br /> Pants, Well, I think the archetype is more the &quot;wise one of the wilds&quot;, the sort of witch figure you go to for wisdom when all else fails, but essentially yes. It's kind of awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T07:52:26-07:00","id":567930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/567387-second-edition-elementals?p=567926#post567926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Raven, you don't see how someone becoming part of a living world and effectively ripping themselves off and running the hell away akin to the skin on your left knee just yanking itself off and slopping across the floor is an effective form of escape?</div> </div> </div> </div> Ah I missed that bit; I didn't notice it said you get awesome element powers to escape with.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T07:59:03-07:00","id":567940,"title":"","content":"It does, effectively, in the last bit of The Escape.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T08:35:49-07:00","id":568009,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Verdana, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Now i want to see an Elemental Singing Let It Go</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T08:43:52-07:00","id":568038,"title":"","content":"So an Elemental escaping from the mines would, for a brief moment, become the mine. They'd extend themselves endlessly, breaching the Hedge, and then tumbling into the mortal world, as a cavernous rocky humanoid, whose voice sounds like it's coming from miles away down in the deep.<br /> <br /> It's less explicit than it could be. That's essentially what I was getting at. It's hard to imagine elementals escaping if they're not doing Elemental kith stuff. But it can be done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5408-fetfet","name":"fetfet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5408_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T08:56:08-07:00","id":568046,"title":"","content":"Remember, this is Arcadia, where &quot;blending into the background&quot; and&quot; becoming part of the scenery&quot; are not just turns of phrase, they're literal transformations. The act of abandoning your ego and becoming one with your environment is a means of escape, because the Wyrd transforms you into an embodiment of the environment. That gives you a way to sneak away, or a new means of locomotion your Keeper might not have accounted for.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/567387-second-edition-elementals?p=567626#post567626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Slave in the underground mines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Become one with the minerals you mine, get carted out with the rest of the gold and make your escape through the hedge once you're safely out of the mines.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/567387-second-edition-elementals?p=567626#post567626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cotton picker in a southern plantation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Become as light as the cotton you pick and escape on the breeze.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/567387-second-edition-elementals?p=567626#post567626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Turned into a loyal robot in a space opera.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interface with the ship's computer. Cease being an individual automoton and become the blinking lights, the hums and whirrs and beeps that control everything in this scifi hellscape. As an extension of the technology that runs your Keepers world, you can easily cause a distraction that will allow you to slip away in an escape pod.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T09:15:32-07:00","id":568055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/567387-second-edition-elementals?p=567626#post567626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm really having trouble understanding how Elementals escaped. Could someone provide examples; lets say the following three durance:<br /> <br /> Slave in the underground mines.<br /> Cotton picker in a southern plantation.<br /> Turned into a loyal robot in a space opera.<br /> <br /> For those can someone describe an escape that would create an Elemental?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> 1 - Crush the guards with a cave in, dig your way to freedom.<br /> <br /> 2 - Alright, no idea... burn the field, maybe?<br /> <br /> 3 - Destroy all meat bags, destroy all meat bags!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T09:20:01-07:00","id":568058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/567387-second-edition-elementals?p=568055#post568055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 3 - Destroy all meat bags, destroy all meat bags!</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds more like the Ogre method.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T09:21:18-07:00","id":568059,"title":"","content":"Hmm, maybe they transmit their consciousness to other machines in the form of a virus and escape by hopping from one body to the next?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T09:25:39-07:00","id":568060,"title":"","content":"Do you mean they all gain dots Elemental Contracts when they gain their Seemings?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T09:37:01-07:00","id":568085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/567387-second-edition-elementals?p=568060#post568060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you mean they all gain dots Elemental Contracts when they gain their Seemings?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they <i>become the elements</i>. Just like a Beast becomes a wild animal, a Darkling becomes the darkness, a Fairest becomes akin to the Fair Folk, and an Ogre becomes a hulking monster. The Act of taking agency in Arcadia physically changes you, and those changes allow you to escape. In the case of elementals, that agency comes from letting go of the self, becoming instead part of the world around you, which makes camouflage much easier and may have other advantages as well. Contracts are a thing you learn after the fact, to bring a bit of that Arcadian Wyrdness into the mundane world you ran back to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T09:37:48-07:00","id":568087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/567387-second-edition-elementals?p=568060#post568060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you mean they all gain dots Elemental Contracts when they gain their Seemings?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't say 'all' by any means, but it's a possible route, in principle. Remember that the context has changed: each Contract now has some number of affinity Seemings, for which the main Contract does a little something different or extra (members of that Seeming get theirs free when they buy the Contract). Even if a Contract doesn't itself pertain to the elements, it may still have an Elemental affinity &quot;clause,&quot;* which may well manifest as some power over the elements.<br /> <br /> But yeah, in a lot of cases, I don't imagine it would really get into mechanics. Contracts are just one possible way some might want to frame it.<br /> <br /> * As yet, this is just personal terminology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T09:44:01-07:00","id":568095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/567387-second-edition-elementals?p=568085#post568085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, they <i>become the elements</i>. Just like a Beast becomes a wild animal, a Darkling becomes the darkness, a Fairest becomes akin to the Fair Folk, and an Ogre becomes a hulking monster. The Act of taking agency in Arcadia physically changes you, and those changes allow you to escape. In the case of elementals, that agency comes from letting go of the self, becoming instead part of the world around you, which makes camouflage much easier and may have other advantages as well. Contracts are a thing you learn after the fact, to bring a bit of that Arcadian Wyrdness into the mundane world you ran back to.</div> </div> </div> </div>How do I interpret this, then:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/567387-second-edition-elementals?p=567556#post567556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They don't need magical powers for that. They escaped on their own. That's something they've got, and that can't be taken away from them. Nobody gave it to them; that was all them.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T09:52:35-07:00","id":568099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/567387-second-edition-elementals?p=568095#post568095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do I interpret this, then:</div> </div> </div> </div>Bro I'm not sure if you know how the context of that conversation went but you had specifically asked about Seeming Blessings and why Clarity of Forces didn't provide a mechanical advantage outside of Clarity recovery.<br /> <br /> Do you think the description of Ogres removing their hearts is not to some degree magical? Arcadian metaph[or/ys]ical shenanigans used to affect the escape do not necessarily translate to permanent supernatural powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T10:21:02-07:00","id":568121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/567387-second-edition-elementals?p=568099#post568099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Bro I'm not sure if you know how the context of that conversation went but you had specifically asked about Seeming Blessings and why Clarity of Forces didn't provide a mechanical advantage outside of Clarity recovery.<br /> <br /> Do you think the description of Ogres removing their hearts is not to some degree magical? Arcadian metaph[or/ys]ical shenanigans used to affect the escape do not necessarily translate to permanent supernatural powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the Ogres, we have: &quot; He reaches into his chest and pulls out his own heart, replacing it with rock or clay so that he becomes, he thinks, invulnerable. Liberated from the part of him that can still hurt, he makes a break for it. He\u2019d been watching, you see, enduring, planning his escape, and now is the moment he goes. He destroys everything in his wake, moving with such brutality and chaos that he can\u2019t be stopped.&quot;<br /> <br /> While the description of the Elementals' escape clearly states: &quot; Quickly, she filled that hole, her heart, herself, with the raw possibility of the elements, embodying fire, electricity, ice, light, any such overwhelming force. And in making that choice, she used the element itself to escaping, becoming it\u2019s child in the real world, free of the Hedge.&quot;<br /> <br /> I can see the Ogres' not so much gaining power but agency, determination and such. The Elementals though? It sounds a whole lot like their literally embodying an element plays a part in their escape. Wether it would be expressed through a Blessin or a Contract'ss clause, this makes me think of a supernatural phenomenon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T10:24:37-07:00","id":568124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/567387-second-edition-elementals?p=567888#post567888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't like the idea that you can only become an Elemental if the Durance allows it. I can think of a way the mine slave who's kept in place because of chains and guards could become any other seeming:<br /> <br /> Darkling - betray another slave in order to escape.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>How very <i><b>Jaime Lannister </b></i>of you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T10:27:15-07:00","id":568127,"title":"","content":"Temporary surges of extreme fae being are not an unusual affair for Changeling backstories. Elementals did a similar thing in 1E, it just now a little bit more of a tight rope.<br /> <br /> THe point being, just because they became the thing in Arcadia doesn't mean they retain that ability once they step out into the less flexible Hedge. Their malleability is, in and of itself, an ocean surge, pulling along one way before going back and equalizing. You get one brief period to be the element before the demands on your ego snap back to bring back in your sense of individuality. You will, from then on, be marked as a child, but until you learn the contract, you're not pulling that trick again.<br /> <br /> It's wibbly wobbly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T10:39:18-07:00","id":568133,"title":"","content":"I would guess that an Elemental becoming one with their element in order to escape is, in a sense, metaphorical. To use a familiar analogy, when Batman says &quot;I am the night,&quot; what he means is that he has taken it upon himself to embody the silent menace of darkness, and so forth. <br /> <br /> However, because Faerie operates on a sort of dream logic, metaphors might take on a literal reality. During their escape, an Elemental might literally become one with the night, but that transformation would be a function of Faerie itself, rather than any innate power that the Changeling has. Once they leave Faerie, &quot;I am the night&quot; goes back to being mostly a metaphor, unless they develop a specific power to make it more than that.<br /> <br /> At least, I think that's the kind of thing they were going for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T10:47:22-07:00","id":568140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/567387-second-edition-elementals?p=568121#post568121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the Ogres, we have: &quot; He reaches into his chest and pulls out his own heart, replacing it with rock or clay so that he becomes, he thinks, invulnerable. Liberated from the part of him that can still hurt, he makes a break for it. He\u2019d been watching, you see, enduring, planning his escape, and now is the moment he goes. He destroys everything in his wake, moving with such brutality and chaos that he can\u2019t be stopped.&quot;<br /> <br /> While the description of the Elementals' escape clearly states: &quot; Quickly, she filled that hole, her heart, herself, with the raw possibility of the elements, embodying fire, electricity, ice, light, any such overwhelming force. And in making that choice, she used the element itself to escaping, becoming it\u2019s child in the real world, free of the Hedge.&quot;<br /> <br /> I can see the Ogres' not so much gaining power but agency, determination and such. The Elementals though? It sounds a whole lot like their literally embodying an element plays a part in their escape. Wether it would be expressed through a Blessin or a Contract'ss clause, this makes me think of a supernatural phenomenon.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is reading it too literally. The Ogre cuts off his ability to feel the hurt, which manifests metaphorically as removing his heart and replacing it with something unfeeling. The Elemental realizes that he is simply another part of a vibrant world and opens himself to it, which manifests metaphorically as welcoming a part of that world into himself. Neither Changeling receives supernatural powers relevant to the respective act.* They're metaphors for the personal change and development the Lost just went through in reclaiming themselves, and manifest physically because that's how Arcadia works.<br /> <br /> That's the baseline, though. As Arc says, sometimes power can come of it. But if any does, it's not generally going to last.* There's power to a Changeling taking back her life in a way like that, and -- place of metaphor that it is -- Arcadia responds to that. But in terms of overt power, it's like an adrenaline surge: maybe for the duration, the Ogre becomes as literally invulnerable as he believes and the Elemental becomes as literally an extension of the world as he believes. It's not really something either can call upon again quite so &quot;easily.&quot;<br /> <br /> * Unless the player chooses to say it does and fluffs it as realizing a particular Contract or takes a particular Merit or something. It's just not the baseline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T11:19:45-07:00","id":568200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/567387-second-edition-elementals?p=568121#post568121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For the Ogres, we have: &amp;quot; He reaches into his chest and pulls out his own heart, replacing it with rock or clay so that he becomes, he thinks, invulnerable. Liberated from the part of him that can still hurt, he makes a break for it. He\u2019d been watching, you see, enduring, planning his escape, and now is the moment he goes. He destroys everything in his wake, moving with such brutality and chaos that he can\u2019t be stopped.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> While the description of the Elementals' escape clearly states: &amp;quot; Quickly, she filled that hole, her heart, herself, with the raw possibility of the elements, embodying fire, electricity, ice, light, any such overwhelming force. And in making that choice, she used the element itself to escaping, becoming it\u2019s child in the real world, free of the Hedge.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> I can see the Ogres' not so much gaining power but agency, determination and such. The Elementals though? It sounds a whole lot like their literally embodying an element plays a part in their escape. Wether it would be expressed through a Blessin or a Contract'ss clause, this makes me think of a supernatural phenomenon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Arcadia does not distinguish between agency and power. The ogre becomes both emotionally invulnerable and physically enduring. The elemental becomes both psychologically mercurial and physically mutable. It doesn't need to be reflected in game mechanics because Arcadia doesn't follow the same rules that the mundane world does, and Changeling is generally played in the mundane world and the hedge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T12:17:07-07:00","id":568240,"title":"","content":"The slave is weak. You are weak. If you were strong you would not be bound with brass and steel. Brass and steel are strong. Give up on yourself. There is no more you. You are brass and steel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T13:51:47-07:00","id":568337,"title":"","content":"Can someone post some examples of this &quot;Apparent chaos given purpose and/or meaning&quot;? I'm a little lost by it, especially the 'reverse causality' bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T14:38:57-07:00","id":568394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/567387-second-edition-elementals?p=568337#post568337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can someone post some examples of this &quot;Apparent chaos given purpose and/or meaning&quot;? I'm a little lost by it, especially the 'reverse causality' bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Reverse causality&quot; could maybe be phrased differently, but I suspect the idea is just making the observation of purpose or meaning in hindsight.<br /> <br /> Anyway, shot in the dark...<br /> <br /> &quot;Ha! You gave me a really hard time for making us three hours late. But if I hadn't, we'd all be dead! Vindicated!&quot;<br /> &quot;I-- <i>You didn't know that</i>! You just didn't want to cut out your 'social night' and forgot to set your alarm!&quot;<br /> &quot;And where'd that apparent irresponsibility and negligence get us? Not dead! Vin. Di. Cated!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T14:47:52-07:00","id":568402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/567387-second-edition-elementals?p=568337#post568337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can someone post some examples of this &amp;quot;Apparent chaos given purpose and/or meaning&amp;quot;? I'm a little lost by it, especially the 'reverse causality' bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, when I play fighting games like Street Fighter and the like, I have no idea what I'm doing. I literally just push buttons at random and hope for the best. Sometimes, I win. That's a small scale example of the kind of thing that Elementals gain Clarity for. When they take chaotic actions and get a positive result from it, they regain Clarity. Even if that positive result was not actually the intended result, if the Elemental can link the result to her actions, she can still say &quot;I meant to do that&quot; and it counts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T16:36:55-07:00","id":568497,"title":"","content":"Hmm. Doesn't quite seem to have that ring of 'elemental power/fury' that I would have expected...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T16:50:09-07:00","id":568500,"title":"","content":"A homeless Elemental lights a fire in a park to keep warm, said fire loses control and burns down half the Park. Elemental finds out he saved a young man from being gangraped when said fire scared his attackers away burning down the Park=chaos, but something good came out of it, saving the young man from his attackers.<br /> <br /> Another Elemental decides to throw a party at her place, one this happens after another and it manages to turn into a chaotic orgy. Nine months later a baby is born from this, new life created, giving the Chaos meaning.<br /> <br /> Another Elemental is a Postman, who fucks up and delivers bills to the wrong people, Chaos insues. But when the poor people get togther to exchange bills and letters, many become friends, meaning from chaos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T17:00:32-07:00","id":568510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/567387-second-edition-elementals?p=568497#post568497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. Doesn't quite seem to have that ring of 'elemental power/fury' that I would have expected...</div> </div> </div> </div>Well like I said, my example was small-scale. Also, the positive result of the chaos doesn't <i>have</i> to be unintended, it just <i>can</i> be. An elemental who kills a huntsman by luring it into his apartment and then blowing up the building could probably gain Clarity from that (assuming Huntsmen can die from something like that, obviously). But they could also gain it for blowing up a building that happened to have a Huntsman in it. The important thing is getting positive results from causing chaos. Whether or not those results were planned is irrelevant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T17:11:43-07:00","id":568515,"title":"","content":"Alright, Elemental time! <br /> <br /> I notice there's a theme of literal heartlessness going on with the Seemings, it's an interesting bit of flavor. Initially I was expecting a bit more of a quiet detachment, but I figure that probably doesn't gel quite as well with the agency themes as the more proactive approach does. It skirts kind of close to the Beast purview, but I think it more-or-less works, considering the relationship the two Seemings have. The Blessing is interesting, the Curse I'm a bit curious about the specifics of, but I get the gist of it. Overall I like it and am interested to see how the final draft comes out.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Also minor sidenote, but the sentence &quot;In that moment, she decided to release her ego, her need to be special vanished in an instant, and her heart fell out, hitting the ground, and shattering to a thousand useless pieces all at once.&quot; feels really weird to me. It might just be a grammar thing (in which case ignore this) but something feels off.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/567387-second-edition-elementals?p=568497#post568497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. Doesn't quite seem to have that ring of 'elemental power/fury' that I would have expected...</div> </div> </div> </div>I had the exact opposite reaction, tbh. I was initially concerned people might see the focus on intensity as overlapping with Beasts, but that doesn't seem to be happening so cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T17:34:21-07:00","id":568521,"title":"","content":"I think the big difference between Elementals and Beasts is that Elementals let go of themselves, while Beasts let go of everyone else. Abandoning individuality as opposed to abandoning society. It's an interesting sort of duality they've got going, like they're two sides of the same coin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T17:42:05-07:00","id":568525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/567387-second-edition-elementals?p=568402#post568402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, when I play fighting games like Street Fighter and the like, I have no idea what I'm doing. I literally just push buttons at random and hope for the best. Sometimes, I win. That's a small scale example of the kind of thing that Elementals gain Clarity for. When they take chaotic actions and get a positive result from it, they regain Clarity. Even if that positive result was not actually the intended result, if the Elemental can link the result to her actions, she can still say &quot;I meant to do that&quot; and it counts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just have to say, your button mashing example is brilliant and made my morning. <br /> <br /> Mostly because last night, my eight year old totally beat me at SF4.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T17:46:15-07:00","id":568526,"title":"","content":"So. Reverse causality. There's a thing I used to do when playing elder vampires in LARPs. I can't hope to accurately portray the experiences and genius of a 600 year old scheming monster. There's no fucking way. But, I had a trick. <br /> <br /> Basically, I would do a lot of random shit. I would take actions with my Resources, Contacts, and whatever that were certainly actions, but barely sensitive to the context. My Storyteller would be like, &quot;Are you sure you want to do this? It's a waste of your Merit for the month.&quot; Or similar. I'd say yes. I'd keep notes about these weird things I did. Then, when fortune turned in my direction, like when the Primogen council elected my character Prince, I would look back at my notes and explain &quot;why&quot; that happened, because of my random actions. <br /> <br /> Or, if you want another example, Dirk Gently's Holistic Detective Agency.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T18:23:30-07:00","id":568568,"title":"","content":"....When a changeling takes on their Seeming (of any kind), does their heart invariably break (which is what really allows them to escape)? If so, can they get it back and/or be made whole again later?<br /> <br /> I ask because I've seen it specifically mentioned in a couple of Seemings, but I don't remember if they all do.<br /> <br /> And I'd like something about Fetches next.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T18:28:58-07:00","id":568574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/567387-second-edition-elementals?p=568568#post568568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">....When a changeling takes on their Seeming (of any kind), does their heart invariably break (which is what really allows them to escape)? If so, can they get it back and/or be made whole again later?</div> </div> </div> </div>More on that later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T18:31:41-07:00","id":568577,"title":"","content":"I think I'm gonna need an example to really get the Curse. Why does realizing that other people have a &quot;me&quot; cause you problems? Is it like Katrina having a blast raining on everyone, and then noticing all the dead bodies from flooding New Orleans and realizing that, &quot;...Whoops, I shouldn't have done that.&quot; or something? Something that reminds you that you're still a human with feelings? Or am I totally not getting this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T18:31:55-07:00","id":568578,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure they've all mentioned it, and I'm pretty sure the pieces of their hearts are what were referred to as &quot;Icons&quot; in the outline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T18:49:48-07:00","id":568599,"title":"","content":"I just wanted to drop in and say that this write-up almost immediately made me want to play an Elemental. This is fantastic. I particularly liked the part describing them as dangersexy. I have this amusing image in mind of an Elemental who keeps finding out after the fact that everyone they hook up with is an extreme sports enthusiast (idea: a Freehold that uses &quot;storm chaser&quot; as slang for both someone turned on by Elementals and potential troublemakers for essentially the same reason). The cold iron Curse is interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T18:54:05-07:00","id":568600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/567387-second-edition-elementals?p=568060#post568060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you mean they all gain dots Elemental Contracts when they gain their Seemings?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, Arcadia is just that fluid in nature. It obeys narrative. It only needs to be represented in the form of a Contract if you still have that exact ability outside of Arcadia, where the air is not inherently inclined to pick you up and carry you away because seized your own story and rewrote yourself as the breeze.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T18:55:02-07:00","id":568602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/567387-second-edition-elementals?p=568525#post568525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I just have to say, your button mashing example is brilliant and made my morning. <br /> <br /> Mostly because last night, my eight year old totally beat me at SF4.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice! Yeah, I am absolutely terrible at fighting games. Except Soul Calibur 2, which I put a ridiculous amount of time in on back in the day. I knew Nightmare's move set like the back of my hand and I practiced the timing on Guard Impacts to the point where I could Guard Impact other players' Guard Impacts. I actually once got into a Guard Impact war with a friend who was similarly obsessed with that game that went on for a good 10 seconds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 06-25-2015, 10:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T19:14:13-07:00","id":568661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/567387-second-edition-elementals?p=568577#post568577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I'm gonna need an example to really get the Curse. Why does realizing that other people have a &quot;me&quot; cause you problems? Is it like Katrina having a blast raining on everyone, and then noticing all the dead bodies from flooding New Orleans and realizing that, &quot;...Whoops, I shouldn't have done that.&quot; or something? Something that reminds you that you're still a human with feelings? Or am I totally not getting this?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> That would seem to make sense. While they may embody the elements of nature, they're still sentient beings. A storm might tear through the trailer park without a second thought, but if you do the same thing and can't justify your reasons for doing so, then what's left of your humanity cracks down on you with a firm reminder that you're not a tornado. Speaking of tornadoes, I'd love to see a wind Elemental who uses a contract that grants supernatural strength. They start flinging cars at a Huntsman like they were tiny rocks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T19:52:45-07:00","id":568682,"title":"","content":"Also, for next week?<br /> <br /> I vote Oneriomancy-I love the idea of dream-shaping, and given Beast spoilers I want to know what the heck a Bastion is. And learn what the new version of dream poisoning is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T20:08:23-07:00","id":568687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/567387-second-edition-elementals?p=568578#post568578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure they've all mentioned it</div> </div> </div> </div>Hunh, I actually thought the word hadn't come up in every Seeming. But on a reread, yeah: the Changeling's heart gets a mention in every draft we've seen.* Though there are a few differences in presentation. The Beast mention comes offhand as a figure of speech, and it's the only one not to appear during The Escape. The Fairest mention is similar; it does come up during The Escape, but it likewise feels like just a turn of phrase. By contrast, the Darkling, Ogre, and Elemental mentions all speak of something literally happening to or involving their Hearts during their escapes, all or parts of them left behind. In the Darkling write-up, it's a consequence of their decision and doesn't really impact the escape itself, whereas in the Ogre and Elemental drafts it's an unmistakably physical and active thing that happened, integrated into the actual and metaphorical sides of the action.<br /> <br /> I really, really like the idea of a unifying thematic to the write-ups, where something significant and explicit happens to a Changeling's heart as part of the escape. I just find it such an evocative element in the Darkling, Ogre, and Elemental write-ups -- the latter two in particular -- whereas I'd honestly forgotten it was mentioned at all in the Beast and Fairest drafts until I went looking for them. That said, I hardly consider this a priority. It would be cool, but only as long as making this particular element ubiquitous doesn't come at the expense of those write-ups. Which I could see as a very real danger.<br /> <br /> *<br /> <u>Beasts:</u> in the introduction, &quot;They\u2019ve got wild eyes and untamed hearts.&quot;<br /> <u>Darklings:</u> in the introduction, &quot;The Darkling carries a broken heart, either their own or shards of someone else\u2019s.&quot; In The Escape, &quot;She decided, in that key moment, that the righteous are fools or liars, and she would be neither. But it broke her heart into a thousand shards, glinting in the shadows around her.&quot;<br /> <u>Fairest:</u> in The Escape, &quot;The Fairest has a change of heart, and changes the hearts and minds of those around him, and in that moment, he escapes.&quot;<br /> <u>Ogres:</u> in The Escape, &quot;He reaches into his chest and pulls out his own heart, replacing it with rock or clay so that he becomes, he thinks, invulnerable.&quot;<br /> Elementals: in The Escape, &quot;In that moment, she decided to release her ego, her need to be special vanished in an instant, and her heart fell out, hitting the ground, and shattering to a thousand useless pieces all at once. Quickly, she filled that hole, her heart, herself, with the raw possibility of the elements, embodying fire, electricity, ice, light, any such overwhelming force.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm pretty sure the pieces of their hearts are what were referred to as &quot;Icons&quot; in the outline. </div> </div> </div>I'm still wondering if the &quot;Icons&quot; might be something else, but that's one of the stronger theories I've heard. I don't know if that'd be the only way they manifest, though: it's possible to escape without a Seeming, but I presume such Changelings still leave Icons in the Hedge. Of course, perhaps Icons can be made in different ways: the Changeling's abandoned/shattered/whatever heart sounds like a very strong candidate for a way an Icon might form. Regardless, we know so little. I'm definitely interested in hearing more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T20:30:48-07:00","id":568696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/567387-second-edition-elementals?p=568578#post568578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure they've all mentioned it, and I'm pretty sure the pieces of their hearts are what were referred to as &quot;Icons&quot; in the outline.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just want to say: Amazing catch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T21:09:47-07:00","id":568738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/567387-second-edition-elementals?p=567608#post567608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They'll also affect affinity Contracts. I wouldn't downplay free Clarity as &quot;purely mental&quot;. It's pretty significant.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Do the former Seeming Blessings survive in Contract form?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T21:26:21-07:00","id":568752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/567387-second-edition-elementals?p=568738#post568738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Do the former Seeming Blessings survive in Contract form?</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. Not really? Frankly, I found the Seeming Blessings to mostly be pretty milquetoast. Spending Glamour for 9-again on a specific roll or adding a Specialty just never did it for me. But I guess ones that add a few dice to certain trait rolls might in certain capacities?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T21:30:22-07:00","id":568754,"title":"","content":"On Icons: I somehow completely forgot all about that.<br /> <br /> I feel a little off kilter now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T22:04:15-07:00","id":568795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/567387-second-edition-elementals?p=568752#post568752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh. Not really? Frankly, I found the Seeming Blessings to mostly be pretty milquetoast. Spending Glamour for 9-again on a specific roll or adding a Specialty just never did it for me. But I guess ones that add a few dice to certain trait rolls might in certain capacities?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, that's pretty much what I meant... like perhaps Fairest get Social pool glamour-surges out of Vainglory that others can't; and Ogres the same for Strength out of Stone; etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T22:15:41-07:00","id":568803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/567387-second-edition-elementals?p=568696#post568696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I just want to say: Amazing catch.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, thank you! I would have mentioned it sooner, but I thought it was a given, what with your description of Icons as parts of the Changeling that got left behind in her escape and the Seemings mentioning loss of their hearts. I think Omegaphallic also mentioned the idea that a Darkling's heart would make a good Icon back when they were first previewed, but the comment probably got buried under King's Raven's and my debate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T22:42:52-07:00","id":568816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/567387-second-edition-elementals?p=567888#post567888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't like the idea that you can only become an Elemental if the Durance allows it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That wasn't what I was saying at all. The Seeming, IMO, isn't just &quot;how you escape&quot;; it's also &quot;how you interpret your Durance&quot;.<br /> <br /> A Beast interprets the Durance as the trappings of civilization; thus it makes sense that that's what he leaves behind in his Escape. Etc., etc. (way too tired to write-up all five right now)<br /> <br /> The point is ultimately that regaining your agency is as much about choosing your perspective, choosing your role in the narrative, choosing how you break the existing story to write a new one, as it is the physical details of the escape. Otherwise, the social and mental consequences of your escape wouldn't be relevant.<br /> <br /> This is why the pre-Durance background is relevant to the Seeming description. What <i>kind</i> of person would choose to interpret their Durance as a trap of their own ego and release that in order to Escape? Someone who already thinks like that. You become an Elemental because you're set up to see the world that way, even before the Faeries found you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T06:05:47-07:00","id":569117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/567387-second-edition-elementals?p=568009#post568009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Now i want to see an Elemental Singing Let It Go</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>And it will be totally in accord with Elementals write-up becuase Elsa is typical your Ice (Queen) Elemental that &quot;Let it Go&quot; after the Durance under her sister and courts as Keepers. She just become one with Ice, and escape to be free.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elemntals preview</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">She spent her life holding it in, hiding what she knew herself to be, to protect her friends and her family. Things are different now. She\u2019ll burn them all with the bitter cold inside of her. She\u2019ll create her own world of ice and snow where she\u2019s completely free, and who cares who freezes to death in the process.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=moSFlvxnbgk\" data-code=\"moSFlvxnbgk\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/moSFlvxnbgk/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-27-2015, 06:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T11:20:14-07:00","id":569448,"title":"","content":"So, re-reading the background, and all the talk of being the biggest fish in a small pond before meeting someone even bigger... Maybe it's low-hanging fruit, but I think Edward Bloom is actually a really good example of an Elemental. He's stuck in Arcadia through almost the entire film, unable to let go of his need to be the most special, interesting person he knows. Will, his Fae-Touched son, struggles to reach his abducted father and bring him back but can't cut through the hedge of Eddy's fantastical stories, until the end when he finally gets through to his father in the hospital and they escape together through a story of Will's telling, with Eddy letting go of his ego and becoming the fish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T12:53:35-07:00","id":569501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/567387-second-edition-elementals?p=569117#post569117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And it will be totally acording to the Elemntlas write-up becuase Elsa is typical your Ice (Queen) Elemental that &quot;Let it Go&quot; after the Durance under her sister and courts as Keepers. She just become one with Ice, and escape to be free.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=moSFlvxnbgk\" data-code=\"moSFlvxnbgk\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/moSFlvxnbgk/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Let it burn, let it burn!<br /> <br /> I am one with the flames and ash!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T20:36:02-07:00","id":569890,"title":"","content":"<i>Let it burn, let it burn! <br /> I am one with the ash and flame!<br /> Let it burn, let it burn!<br /> I'll never be the same!<br /> <br /> Now I see<br /> What mistakes I've made...<br /> And I know I've paid...</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T20:42:27-07:00","id":569892,"title":"","content":"It probably says something that the two kiths I want to try to work with for Elementals at the moment are a Razorhand and a Gravewight. Clarity of Forces goes a long way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T23:05:48-07:00","id":569986,"title":"","content":"I'm ambivalent about the apparent focus on the violent and intense. It's all storms and fires and hurricanes and such. &quot;Quickly, she filled that hole, her heart, herself, with the raw possibility of the elements, embodying <i>fire, electricity, ice, light, any such overwhelming force</i>.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'd shrug and say I can ignore those parts of the flavor text if I want to make a calmer or more sedate Elemental, but then there's the Blessing... I'll have to think on it a bit more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T23:14:27-07:00","id":569989,"title":"","content":"Yes, because earth and wood are such sedate and predictable forces.<br /> <br /> Okay, comparatively they are, but still.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T03:56:40-07:00","id":570111,"title":"","content":"To be honest, all my reading was influenced by my thinking &quot;can I redo this one particular character in 2e?&quot;<br /> <br /> In first edition, character is a singer. (The original idea that sparked the character was actually &quot;what about someone abducted to serve as a musician or singer or something, but who isn't a Fairest?&quot;) Whenever they displease their keeper, they get put into an iron coffin and chucked into a fire for a while. Eventually, they melt and turn into a statue of glass. Then escape at some point afterward. A mix of horrifying torture with weird fairy tale logic, plus interesting powers in play. The one bad thing is that none of the Elemental kiths actually fit.<br /> <br /> With 2e, there's the advantage that you can just take the Artist kith. But the new interpretation on Seemings necessitates some re-imagining. So. New version. Turning into glass wasn't just something that happened at some point: it's how they escaped. The character leaves behind human frailty, turns into unfeeling matter and oozes away from their Keeper's clutches. Since then I've been waiting for the Elemental spoiler to drop so I can compare. (It's just my luck that the one Seeming I was waiting for the most was almost the last one shown.) And... The Escape is great. Almost perfect, really, if you remove the references to big wild nature and overwhelming forces. &quot;Or maybe she went dim, fading, beginning to become nothing since she could never hope to matter anymore. And yet, at some point, brutal winds toughened her skin, or else the pain of hot steel dimmed and she felt only the sensation, not the agony. [...] In that moment, she decided to release her ego, her need to be special vanished in an instant, and her heart fell out, hitting the ground, and shattering to a thousand useless pieces all at once. Quickly, she filled that hole, her heart, herself, with the raw possibility of the elements [...]. And in making that choice, she used the element itself in escaping, becoming its child in the real world, free of the Hedge.&quot; Great. Except... there's no storm inside, no grand desert or earthquake, nothing great and terrible, nothing to lure in adrenaline junkies, no whimsical chaos and destruction.<br /> <br /> So: ambivalent. It reads well, but isn't quite what I was expecting. Since then I've been alternating between thinking about the character and wondering if my &quot;complaint&quot; is just a personal matter or if it genuinely closes down interesting options. Ice... snowstorms. Rock... earthquakes. Should rock and earth necessarily mean earthquakes and landslides and such? A great, ancient tree isn't really known for &quot;whim and devastation&quot; and &quot;throwing caution to the wind&quot;... Metal? Is metal chaotic with &quot;order behind the destruction&quot;?<br /> <br /> There were some fire elemental Contracts, maybe I should play up that part. The caged-in heat from the character's rebirth. Or maybe I should just go with an odd Ogre who happens to look glassy, they also have themes of protecting yourself from pain... Although the violence Blessing doesn't really fit either...<br /> <br /> And so on and so forth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":815,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","user":"Kazorh","date":". 06-27-2015, 07:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T09:43:46-07:00","id":570310,"title":"","content":"It's worth remembering that there is a chaotic element to creation as well.<br /> <br /> But more to point, these are a set of archetypes. Be flexible in your reading and permit the stories to flux to your needs.<br /> <br /> More or less how WoD has worked up to this point anyways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T10:42:30-07:00","id":570335,"title":"","content":"It occurs to me that Elementals make great mad scientist types, just doing whatever strange experiment pops into their head and seeing what comes of it, only tangentially caring who gets hurt or what boundaries are transgressed in the name of Science.<br /> <br /> Elemental Hedgespinning mad scientist, bam, got my first 2e Lost antagonist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T15:13:20-07:00","id":570630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/567387-second-edition-elementals?p=568526#post568526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or, if you want another example, Dirk Gently's Holistic Detective Agency.</div> </div> </div> </div>Never had the pleasure. Care to clarify?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T15:38:44-07:00","id":570651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/567387-second-edition-elementals?p=570630#post570630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Never had the pleasure. Care to clarify?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a novel by Douglas Adams, and one of my favorites. It's an odd book (though the author may have tipped you off). I heartily recommend it, and I'm probably overdo for a reread, come to think of it.<br /> <br /> Here are some quotes from the novel. I think Dirk says most of them, though I believe the last is the narrator's observation about him.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dirk Gently's Holistic Detective Agency</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u201cI'm very glad you asked me that, Mrs Rawlinson. The term `holistic' refers to my conviction that what we are concerned with here is the fundamental interconnectedness of all things. I do not concern myself with such petty things as fingerprint powder, telltale pieces of pocket fluff and inane footprints. I see the solution to each problem as being detectable in the pattern and web of the whole. The connections between causes and effects are often much more subtle and complex than we with our rough and ready understanding of the physical world might naturally suppose, Mrs Rawlinson.<br /> <br /> &quot;Let me give you an example. If you go to an acupuncturist with toothache he sticks a needle instead into your thigh. Do you know why he does that, Mrs Rawlinson?<br /> <br /> No, neither do I, Mrs Rawlinson, but we intend to find out. A pleasure talking to you, Mrs Rawlinson. Goodbye.\u201d <hr /><br /> \u201cThe complexities of cause and effect defy analysis.\u201d <hr /><br /> \u201cSherlock Holmes observed that once you have eliminated the impossible then whatever remains, however improbable, must be the answer. I, however, do not like to eliminate the impossible.\u201d <hr /><br /> \u201cI commend you on your skepticism, but even the skeptical mind must be prepared to accept the unacceptable when there is no alternative. If it looks like a duck, and quacks like a duck, we have at least to consider the possibility that we have a small aquatic bird of the family Anatid\u00e6 on our hands.\u201d <hr /><br /> \u201c...was friend the word? He seemed more like a succession of extraordinary events than a person.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T16:17:56-07:00","id":570669,"title":"","content":"Elementals are looking good, going to go back and look at the others before I develop any particular preferences, though.<br /> <br /> Maybe once I figure out which seeming to go with, I'll talk a bit about a character I've been wanting to play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Currently Playing:</b> <i>A large, mixed splat game of <b>CofD</b>.</i> <b>As:</b> Seraph du Salomon, Voice on the concordance. Unsubtle man reluctantly participating in the business of Magi. Awakening 2E homebrew <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1338514-house-du-salomon-a-proximus-dynasty?_=1569864567692\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...=1569864567692</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","name":"Gryphon's Feather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2598_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"215"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T21:32:27-07:00","id":570894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/567387-second-edition-elementals?p=570310#post570310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But more to point, these are a set of archetypes. Be flexible in your reading and permit the stories to flux to your needs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can't really be flexible about my reading of the Blessing unless I want to houserule a new one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T21:40:15-07:00","id":570900,"title":"","content":"Then let's provide context. Elementals are the Eye of the Storm. Maybe they are the eye because they deeply understand it by being the storm, the wildfire, the thunderstorm, the flash flood. Maybe they are the eye because they are divorced from it, the calm tree, the solid rock, the still northern air. Elementals, however divorced they are from humanity, through chaos or stillness can line things up as things happen and know the hidden geometries of the world's breath.<br /> <br /> It's up to you, but they are the people who can make sense of things that would escape everyone else who is too close to the human perspective to understand the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T22:17:48-07:00","id":570980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/567387-second-edition-elementals?p=570894#post570894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can't really be flexible about my reading of the Blessing unless I want to houserule a new one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe your character gains Clarity from the Blessing because she takes a wider view than more individualistic people. She sees the order in seemingly random acts of nature, and that knowledge brings her comfort. Maybe she doesn't have the storm inside herself, but she knows the storm well and she knows that the storm does not simply destroy - it creates potential for renewal. When she finds evidence of that it gives her piece of mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T12:21:06-07:00","id":571728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/567387-second-edition-elementals?p=570651#post570651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a novel by Douglas Adams, and one of my favorites. It's an odd book (though the author may have tipped you off). I heartily recommend it, and I'm probably overdo for a reread, come to think of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, very clever (as expected of an Adams work), but how does that fit in as an example of reverse causality?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T13:16:44-07:00","id":571807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/567387-second-edition-elementals?p=571728#post571728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, very clever (as expected of an Adams work), but how does that fit in as an example of reverse causality?</div> </div> </div> </div>The conventional understanding of causality is that effects are justified by their causes, and thus most people envision an effect and then reverse-engineer the course of action needed to cause it.<br /> <br /> Reverse causality as typified by Clarity of Forces instead justifies causes by their effects, and thus Elementals create a cause which later provides an effect that affirms its necessity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T22:23:06-07:00","id":572216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>fetfet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/567387-second-edition-elementals?p=567417#post567417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the draft - I can see how one could argue than Nate from Leverage is one. The only thing I'm concerned with is that the draft is a bit too focused on the elements. I know that sounds dumb, but what I mean is that you can be a Hunterheart Elemental, or an Artist Elemental. And that kind of stuff isn't well represented, to me. I could be wrong. But it's a strong draft. And that Michael Alig quote is kinda dark.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm honestly not sure I can see Nate as an Elemental. He feels much more like a Darkling, betrayed by his company, he feels like he betrayed his family, he always has a backup plan so he doesn't actually have to trust anyone with anything really important, he sees only the worst in people, it all just lines up really well with the Darklings. He's fairly intense, yes, but that's really the only thing of the Elementals I see in him. He's still got his ego, he was unhappy being a thief, and he never did anything without planning it to hell and back first.<br /> <br /> So I really just don't see it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T22:48:16-07:00","id":572253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/567387-second-edition-elementals?p=572216#post572216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm honestly not sure I can see Nate as an Elemental. He feels much more like a Darkling, betrayed by his company, he feels like he betrayed his family, he always has a backup plan so he doesn't actually have to trust anyone with anything really important, he sees only the worst in people, it all just lines up really well with the Darklings. He's fairly intense, yes, but that's really the only thing of the Elementals I see in him. He's still got his ego, he was unhappy being a thief, and he never did anything without planning it to hell and back first.<br /> <br /> So I really just don't see it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like he's too loyal to his 'new family' to be a Darkling. The only time he endangers them is when he's off the wagon, which is its own monster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T23:20:03-07:00","id":572326,"title":"","content":"I'd also like to add +1 to the people who have noted that the writeup feels too focused on the big, powerful, natural elements. I mean, if I was going to play an Elemental, I'd probably play a Manikin or a Maker that was a living piece of clockwork or something, but that doesn't quite feel like it jives with the writeup as given. Said character would lack ego, sure, but I can't really see her as someone who would be setting off storm warning bells in the minds of others or attracting adrenaline junkies. Nor would she specifically be a character of &quot;whim and devastation.&quot; And I still don't think I quite get the mental aspect of the Curse, so I can't really tell how that would apply either way.<br /> <br /> But, given the whole &quot;big fish in a small pond&quot; thing, I honestly can't see how the Maker Kith is just inherently wrong for the Elementals either. <br /> <br /> The girl who is really big into the Maker/DIY scene, because she's good at it and receives lots of praise for it and knows she's good at it, until a rival comes along and bests her, taking her praise, to the point that she would do anything to get it back. And so she agrees to a strange commission without reading the fine print and ends up in Arcadia, remolded into a Steampunk C&amp;C Machine, creating her masterpieces for her Keeper who holds her until she produces her promised &quot;Ultimate Masterpiece.&quot; She creates many things of unsurpassed skill, but still the Keeper is unsatisfied. It is not until she realizes that her own ego and desire for glory are keeping her too focused on the wrong aspects of design, that she can only create great art once she gives herself to it, body and soul, that she is able to break her heart and transcend her skills, to produce something so wonderful that the Keeper has to agree that it is the promised &quot;ultimate Masterpiece&quot; and allowing her to return home.<br /> <br /> ....Ok, so, maybe you could argue that works better as a Wizened or something, and I'm not entirely sure you can actually escape a Keeper like that, but I think it fits the described Elemental background and durance reasonably well. In her case, the Element would be something like Craft. And, while the resulting changeling would probably be rather obsessed with making things, to the point of ignoring the emotional (and possibly physical) needs of others, she's not likely to attract extreme sports enthusiasts as hangers on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T23:40:22-07:00","id":572363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/567387-second-edition-elementals?p=572253#post572253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel like he's too loyal to his 'new family' to be a Darkling. The only time he endangers them is when he's off the wagon, which is its own monster.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nate takes the long view of things, especially during the first season. They need to trust him to perform properly and, if he wants to keep using them to go after the bad guys, then they need to be kept around and happy. He can push them to their limits, but, if pushes them too far and really endangers them, they'll walk and he'll lose his best tools. Thus, it's logical to keep the plans involving betrayal down towards the bottom.<br /> <br /> ....It's what he keeps telling himself anyway. It's just logic. There's a part of him that still wants to trust back, after all, but he's been burned before and, more importantly, if he trusts them, he'll start treating them like people, instead of tools, which means he'll get emotional at the wrong time and the plan will go south.<br /> <br /> Anyway, even if you still don't buy Nate as a Darkling, I'd rather move the topic back to Elementals and hear your argument for why Nate is one, since I don't really think I get them yet.<br /> <br /> (Thinking on it, Sterling might make a good Darkling too, since he's just in it for himself. Or would he be a Huntsman? Maybe a Loyalist?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T00:16:49-07:00","id":572370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/567387-second-edition-elementals?p=572363#post572363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nate takes the long view of things</div> </div> </div> </div>Cutting in as someone who hasn't seen Leverage and doesn't have the media backlog space to do so for months to come, when you drop a line like this I am immediately confused how you're having trouble understanding the Elemental headspace.<br /> <br /> The Elemental escape is an embracing of the fact that there is a bigger picture that you are equipped to act under the auspices of. It doesn't matter how fast or slow the force you embody is normally \u2014 Arcadian time runs at the speed of plot and those features of Arcadia that aren't warped possessions or tendrils of the Fae are held back from eternal narrative supremacy by the same fairy wordbonding that enables them to turn the tide of legends.<br /> <br /> A briar grows over the battlements of a castle overnight; the earth trembles for an instant and destroys a homestead's livelihood; the tides grind cliffs to sand; these are manifestations of The World at work, and the most familiar fae masks they wear are the ones that resonate with nature, but the funny thing about &quot;nature&quot; is that the concept's Greek/Latin name gives rise to &quot;physics.&quot; The Elemental paradigm leans on the old fae standby of intensity \u2014 a Maker Elemental is not so much an artificer as the raw force of artifice made temporal, and even if humanity at large prefers to remain in the dark about the Fae, they understand on some level that something more concerned with construction than conversation might eventually look at them as obstacles, if not spare parts, and the kind of person who finds that attractive is probably on some level a thrill-seeker regardless of their athletic pursuits.<br /> <br /> An instrument of something <i>bigger than your entire family</i> is walking around living a reasonable facsimile of a normal life. That's going to leave its mark on how they interact with people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T00:25:37-07:00","id":572373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/567387-second-edition-elementals?p=572363#post572363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nate takes the long view of things, especially during the first season. They need to trust him to perform properly and, if he wants to keep using them to go after the bad guys, then they need to be kept around and happy. He can push them to their limits, but, if pushes them too far and really endangers them, they'll walk and he'll lose his best tools. Thus, it's logical to keep the plans involving betrayal down towards the bottom.<br /> <br /> ....It's what he keeps telling himself anyway. It's just logic. There's a part of him that still wants to trust back, after all, but he's been burned before and, more importantly, if he trusts them, he'll start treating them like people, instead of tools, which means he'll get emotional at the wrong time and the plan will go south.<br /> <br /> Anyway, even if you still don't buy Nate as a Darkling, I'd rather move the topic back to Elementals and hear your argument for why Nate is one, since I don't really think I get them yet.<br /> <br /> (Thinking on it, Sterling might make a good Darkling too, since he's just in it for himself. Or would he be a Huntsman? Maybe a Loyalist?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Sterling would be a Huntsman or Loyalist. I could see it both ways. Particularly when you consider the Queen's Gambit Job, he becomes a more or less spot on Huntsman.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T07:44:24-07:00","id":572630,"title":"","content":"I have to admit, I was pretty pessimistic about Changeling 2nd Edition, because I didn't like the way Seemings were changing - in particular, I couldn't see how the Elementals and their kiths (my very favourite part of the old game) were going to fit in. I'm still not entirely on board, but this post has alleviated a lot.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T01:30:46-07:00","id":573660,"title":"","content":"So...<br /> <br /> I did predict some things about Elementals, mainly, the whole letting go of yourself, but it was a lucky guess.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It does open itself up to a lot of variety, which is definitely needed for this Seeming the most, considered how the original worked, so... yeah, great job!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T16:21:58-08:00","id":772607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/567387-second-edition-elementals?p=569892#post569892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It probably says something that the two kiths I want to try to work with for Elementals at the moment are a Razorhand and a Gravewight. Clarity of Forces goes a long way.</div> </div> </div> </div>i'm actually trying to formulate a broadback elemental right now,do you havy any suggestions of the aesthetics?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T17:37:05-08:00","id":772665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/567387-second-edition-elementals?p=772607#post772607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i'm actually trying to formulate a broadback elemental right now,do you havy any suggestions of the aesthetics?</div> </div> </div> </div>Any of the more solid classic-elemental kiths lend themselves well to similar aesthetics \u2014 glaciers, trees, mountains, and other icons of persistence are a good starting point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T18:48:17-08:00","id":772706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/567387-second-edition-elementals?p=772665#post772665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Any of the more solid classic-elemental kiths lend themselves well to similar aesthetics \u2014 glaciers, trees, mountains, and other icons of persistence are a good starting point.</div> </div> </div> </div> The Sun as a symbol might also be incorporated into the Mien. It performs its duty every day, and in Egyptian mythology, Ra (the sun god) fights Apep/Apophis (the chaos god) every day as well. I don't know of any mythologies that associate the Moon with perseverance and hard work, however. A more industrial-looking Mien is also possible, to represent a changeling who was both worker and tool, and could not be distracted as he toiled away in a factory. Technological aspects in the Mien shouldn't be exclusive to Elementals and Wizened, methinks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T02:45:14-08:00","id":772890,"title":"","content":"It seems a little too specific for a seeming. Like, maybe it's just me, but this notion of &quot;your character escaped by letting go of the notion of ego and becoming part of the world around him&quot; sounds like a really significant personality aspect to have decided for me. I haven't read the other seemings, but part of the fun of nWoD (for me, anyway) is playing characters who subvert the expectations associated with whatever they are. A social justice warrior ventrue. A really cheerful and optimistic moros. I can do that because those splats &quot;tend towards&quot; certain things. This reads very much as &quot;this is what an elemental is, and if your character isn't that, then he's not an elemental.&quot; If your character hasn't abandoned his notion of self and attained Buddhist enlightenment, then he's still in Arcadia, friend. Or he's a different seeming. It'd be one thing if it was a bit more generic, like... say... an ogre is an ogre because he escaped through some application of brute force. But there's a lot of detail here that doesn't leave much room for interpretation or my own personal touch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6337-someguywithakatana","name":"someguywithakatana","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T05:44:05-08:00","id":773005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>someguywithakatana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/567387-second-edition-elementals?p=772890#post772890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems a little too specific for a seeming. Like, maybe it's just me, but this notion of &quot;your character escaped by letting go of the notion of ego and becoming part of the world around him&quot; sounds like a really significant personality aspect to have decided for me. I haven't read the other seemings, but part of the fun of nWoD (for me, anyway) is playing characters who subvert the expectations associated with whatever they are. A social justice warrior ventrue. A really cheerful and optimistic moros. I can do that because those splats &quot;tend towards&quot; certain things. This reads very much as &quot;this is what an elemental is, and if your character isn't that, then he's not an elemental.&quot; If your character hasn't abandoned his notion of self and attained Buddhist enlightenment, then he's still in Arcadia, friend. Or he's a different seeming. It'd be one thing if it was a bit more generic, like... say... an ogre is an ogre because he escaped through some application of brute force. But there's a lot of detail here that doesn't leave much room for interpretation or my own personal touch.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not &quot;You're an X Seeming so you have to have X personality&quot;, it's &quot;You're character escaped Arcadia in X manner, so you get Seeming Y&quot;. It's a matter of causality.<br /> <br /> But still, you don't necessarily have to &quot;abandoned his notion of self and attained Buddhist enlightenment&quot;. Your character just as to have sincere realized &quot;This force is greater&quot; and let it inside at the cost of your self... slightly (but importantly) different. You could be a thin wisp of a person and break down and realize how pathetic you are in the grand scale of everything, a speck of dust, become hollow in the grim realization that you aren't and never will matter, and slowly the dust starts to fill you. You could be a warrior, fighting against the ravages of the elements day after day, only just surviving each time an obstacle arises, you have to make sacrifices, it starts with losing the luxuries, but the sacrifices grow and grow until eventually you have to sacrifice part of who you are, you have to kill to survive, you have to give up friendship, you have to give up feeling safe, you have to give up fear, you have to give up your humanity, each sacrifice makes you stronger as something else gets in, and before long you find your flesh replaced with twig and branch.<br /> <br /> The elemental seeming is one of enlightenment, but not Buddhist enlightenment. It is a horrorific, yet primordial type of enlightenment. It is far closer to the tales of Lovecraft than it is Buddhism. <br /> <br /> Also, if you need good 2e Elemental inspiration, read Pact. One of it's characters is nearly exactly a 2e Elemental (except that he lacks a mein and his Curse is slightly different to Burning without Ego).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 11-24-2015, 08:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T06:04:07-08:00","id":773029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/567387-second-edition-elementals?p=773005#post773005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not &quot;You're an X Seeming so you have to have X personality&quot;, it's &quot;You're character escaped Arcadia in X manner, so you get Seeming Y&quot;. It's a matter of causality.<br /> <br /> But still, you don't necessarily have to &quot;abandoned his notion of self and attained Buddhist enlightenment&quot;. Your character just as to have sincere realized &quot;This force is greater&quot; and let it inside at the cost of your self... slightly (but importantly) different. You could be a thin wisp of a person and break down and realize how pathetic you are in the grand scale of everything, a speck of dust, become hollow in the grim realization that you aren't and never will matter, and slowly the dust starts to fill you. You could be a warrior, fighting against the ravages of the elements day after day, only just surviving each time an obstacle arises, you have to make sacrifices, it starts with losing the luxuries, but the sacrifices grow and grow until eventually you have to sacrifice part of who you are, you have to kill to survive, you have to give up friendship, you have to give up feeling safe, you have to give up fear, you have to give up your humanity, each sacrifice makes you stronger as something else gets in, and before long you find your flesh replaced with twig and branch.<br /> <br /> The elemental seeming is one of enlightenment, but not Buddhist enlightenment. It is a horrorific, yet primordial type of enlightenment. It is far closer to the tales of Lovecraft than it is Buddhism.<br /> <br /> Also, if you need good 2e Elemental inspiration, read Pact. One of it's characters is nearly exactly a 2e Elemental (except that he lacks a mein and his Curse is slightly different to Burning without Ego).</div> </div> </div> </div>I appreciate the clarification. I still feel like that's a lot of what my character is about being decided for me, but different strokes and all.<br /> <br /> Edit: Like, take Edition 1. Your seeming is decided by what your keeper made you do while you were in Arcadia, which is what your kith is now. Since that was something out of your control, you could play basically any type of character in any seeming. But now, my seeming is the direct result of a choice my character made, or at the very least of a development of his character. That, by necessity, precludes certain character types from certain seemings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6337,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6337-someguywithakatana","user":"someguywithakatana","date":".  Clarifying my point 11-24-2015, 09:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6337-someguywithakatana","name":"someguywithakatana","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T07:05:31-08:00","id":773075,"title":"","content":"That does sound problematic...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T11:34:49-08:00","id":773278,"title":"","content":"The character can still play against type, while it was a choice the character made, the don't have to continue to think or act the same way. It doesn't preclude anything, it just adds a wrinkle to the backstory of that concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T11:36:13-08:00","id":773280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>someguywithakatana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/567387-second-edition-elementals?p=773029#post773029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I appreciate the clarification. I still feel like that's a lot of what my character is about being decided for me, but different strokes and all.</div> </div> </div> </div>For what it's worth, there is going to be a sidebar in the beginning of the Seemings section that clarifies the fact that the Seemong writeups are just examples of what is typical for a character of a given seeming, not unilateral truths about all members of it. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>someguywithakatana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/567387-second-edition-elementals?p=773029#post773029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: Like, take Edition 1. Your seeming is decided by what your keeper made you do while you were in Arcadia, which is what your kith is now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, what your Keeper did to you or made you do has always determined your Kith. In 1e, Seeming was determined by how or why you were taken. Beasts were innocent people lured into Arcadia by the call of the wild. Darklings were taken as punishment for some (usually unwitting) transgression against the Fae. Elementals were sought out because they possessed some exceptional quality that the Keeper desired or needed. Faerest were taken for their beauty or talent. Ogres were taken for their physical prowess or some character trait made them well-suited to combat or physical labor. Wizened were taken for no reason at all, or at least no reason that makes sense to human logic. I mean, they were all qualified with *mosts* and *usuallies*, but so are the 2e writeups, plus there's the sidebar I mentioned earlier.<br /> <br /> Most people tended to forget that the abduction was the determining factor for Seemings, probably because it was so often skirted around or outright ignored. I imagine groups that want to play Changeling 2e but dislike the new approach to Seemings will do the same.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>someguywithakatana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/567387-second-edition-elementals?p=773029#post773029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Since that was something out of your control, you could play basically any type of character in any seeming. But now, my seeming is the direct result of a choice my character made, or at the very least of a development of his character. That, by necessity, precludes certain character types from certain seemings.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is a slight change of thinking, yes. You have to consider how your character changed herself in order to escape her Durance, and that decision will point towards one or more Seemings that suit that story best. But there's no reason you can't play against type if you really want to. Maybe your character betrayed her best friend in order to escape in his place, which would strongly suggest a Darkling. But if you really liked the idea of this character as an elemental? Well, maybe to her, that betrayal was a symbolic act. Maybe in that moment she realized that the only way she could escape was by betraying herself, her own sense of individual identity. Since Seeming as &quot;how you changed yourself&quot; is such an intensely personal thing, there is a lot of room for flexibility. If what your character took out of the act that freed her was a liberation of ego, who's to say she's not an elemental, regardless of what the act may have looked like from an outside perspective?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}